Langertha::Metrics appears to be a legacy metrics container not used by
Role::Langfuse or Response.usage. Deprecation candidate. The deeper
audit covers Langertha::Usage / Langertha::Pricing / Langertha::Cost /
Langertha::UsageRecord — these are referenced by Response.usage and
need careful back-compat if their attribute shape changes.

Proposed sub-tickets:
  28a — usage stats: determine which of Langertha::Usage, Pricing, Cost,
        UsageRecord are referenced by Response.usage attributes (callers,
        tests). Map field-level usage across providers.
  28b — pricing source-of-truth: identify where per-model pricing
        constants live, when they were last updated, what would break
        if a stale constant is referenced (Langertha::Engine::OpenAI has
        pricing tables — check other engines).
  28c — Metrics deprecation: confirm Langertha::Metrics has zero
        internal callers; remove or formally deprecate with a clear
        timeline.
  28d — Usage shape audit: validate every (engine, capability)
        combination emits a consistent Response.usage.usage block
        (input/output/cache_creation/cache_read/total tokens)
  28e — Pricing drift: spot-check pricing tables against current
        per-provider published pricing — same provider-reality-check
        pattern as karr #23-26.
  28f — Cost calc path: trace UsageRecord → Pricing → Cost resolution;
        ensure back-compat for downstream consumers that read raw
        cost floats.
  28g — tests: usage-shape regressions per engine; pricing-constant
        freshness tests; cost calc roundtrip tests.
  28h — Changes entry: deprecation notice + migration path.
  28i — ADR candidate: ADRs document WHY pricing/constants are not
