## CORRECTION to the per-engine table above (verified in code, 2026-08-11)

Gemini does NOT pass usageMetadata through raw on the non-streaming path —
`Engine::Gemini` normalizes it to prompt_tokens/completion_tokens/total_tokens
and DROPS the camelCase originals. Only the STREAMING path
(Stream::Chunk) carries raw `usageMetadata`. So chat vs. stream disagree on
usage shape within one engine — worth a 28d finding.

Engine::OpenAIResponses likewise normalizes and in doing so DROPS the whole
`input_tokens_details` block, i.e. `cached_tokens` never reaches
Response->usage. Real telemetry hole: Responses API consumers cannot observe
prompt-cache hits at all (related: karr #18e).

